# Expense Claims — Approver (Manager) Functional Context

> Source: Azure DevOps wiki "Digital Channels" → *Channels App / mysdworx app / Functional documentation / Pending Approvals / Claims* (plus shared *Generic approvals* UX patterns, flagged where used). The Claims root page returned no content.
> Scope: manager/approver perspective. Companion to `Claim_FunctionalDoc_Requester`.

## 1. Overview & purpose (approver role)
- Lets a user in a **manager / approver** role review expense claim submissions and **approve or reject** them.
- Available only to users with **approval rights for expense claims**.
- Actions can be taken **inline from the overview** or after **opening claim detail** for a fuller review.
- Approve and reject may require an **approver comment**, depending on configuration.
- Out of scope of the UI pages (stated to live in User Actions / Rules & Behavior): decision logic, validation rules, data loading, permissions, post-decision processing.

## 2. Approvals inbox / Claims approval overview

**Entry points**
- **Pending Approvals tile** on home:
  - Single approval category → **directly to Claims approvals overview**.
  - Multiple categories → **approval categories overview** first; approver selects **Claims**.
- Direct to claim detail from a **notification** (tap / "Review") or the **app inbox** (tap submission card).

**Overview structure**
- Header: page title (e.g. "Expense claims"); back navigation.
- **List of approval cards**, vertically stacked & scrollable — one card per submitted claim (layout similar to grouped expenses / overtime).

**Claim approval card content**
| Field | Notes |
|--|--|
| Employee name | Primary info |
| Total claim amount | Supports **one or multiple currencies** |
| Date of the claim | |

**Card actions**
- Inline **Approve / Reject** on each card (no navigation required).
- Tapping the **card body** opens the **claim detail (approval context)**.
- **Empty state** when no claims await approval.
- Filters / grouping / sorting: not described in the Claims pages.

## 3. Claim detail in approval context
- **Reuses the employee-facing Claim detail screen** — same layout for all claim/expense info.
- Approval-specific differences:
  - **Header shows no actions.**
  - **Bottom action bar** shows **Approve** and **Reject**, always visible while the claim is **Pending approval**.
- Field inventory (individual expenses, amounts, attachments, VAT, dates, net/tax) is inherited from the base employee claim detail and **not re-enumerated** in the approval pages (see gaps).

## 4. Approve action
**Preconditions:** Claim **Pending approval**; approval rights; approver role; claim data retrievable.

**Entry points:** Overview, Notification, App inbox, Claim detail. Behavior is **identical across all entry points** and always approves the **entire claim** (no partial approve).

**Approver comment step (config-driven):**
| Config | Behavior |
|--|--|
| Comment **mandatory** | Must enter a comment to continue |
| Comment **optional** | May enter or continue without |
| Comments **prohibited** | Comment screen skipped → straight to confirmation |

- Comment screen is **free-text**; it does not execute the approval by itself.

**On confirmation (success):**
1. Entire claim approved.
2. Claim **state updated**.
3. Claim **removed from pending approvals**.
4. Requester-side UI reflects updated state.

**On cancel:** no approval; stay on current screen.

**Error handling:**
| Failure | Behavior |
|--|--|
| Backend error | Error shown; claim **remains pending** |
| Network error | Error shown; **retry** available |

## 5. Reject action (incl. partial rejection)
**Preconditions:** Claim **Pending approval**; approval rights; claim contains **≥1 expense**.

**Scope by entry point:**
| Entry point | Reject scope |
|--|--|
| Overview / Notification / App inbox | **Full-claim rejection only** |
| Claim detail screen | **Partial or full** via expense selection |

**Reject from overview / notification / inbox:** Reject → **approver comment screen** → comment (per config) → confirm/cancel. Always **full-claim**.

**Reject from claim detail → Assigned expense rejection selection screen** (shown **only** from detail):
- Open detail → Reject → **expense rejection selection** → select invalid expenses → continue to comment/confirmation.
- Rules:
  - **Multiple expenses selectable.**
  - **At least one expense must be selected to proceed.**
  - Selection state must be **visually explicit**.
  - **Selected = rejected; unselected = (implicitly) approved.**
  - No action executes here; rejection **not final** yet (intent only).
  - **Cancel / Back** abandons, returns to detail, **no changes**.

**Approver comment step (rejection):**
- Comment screen is **always shown** for rejection (all entry points).
- Manager **must provide a rejection reason to continue** (required per the User Action page).
- Free-text; does not execute rejection by itself.
- *Inconsistency:* the Reject overview UI page says the comment screen appears only "when comments are optional or mandatory," while the User Action page says it is *always* shown and a reason is *mandatory* — see gaps.

**On confirmation (success):**
- Selected expenses **rejected**.
- Claim **returned to the employee**.
- Claim **removed from pending approvals**.
- Overview/Notification/Inbox → entire claim rejected; Detail → claim rejected with partial selection.

**On cancel (any step):** no rejection; return to previous screen; **claim remains pending**.

**Error handling:**
| Failure | Behavior |
|--|--|
| Backend error | Error shown; claim remains pending |
| Comment validation error | Feedback shown; rejection **not submitted** |
| Network error | Error shown; retry |

## 6. Notifications & downstream effects on the requester
- **Approve:** claim state updated; requester UI reflects it; claim leaves pending approvals.
- **Reject:** claim **returned to the employee** (with rejected expenses); leaves pending approvals.
- The Claims pages do **not** detail requester-side push/email notification content or what the requester can then do with a returned claim (see gaps).

## 7. Notable rules, edge cases & validations (QA-relevant)
- **Config-driven comment behavior:** test Mandatory (block until entered), Optional (with/without), Prohibited (screen skipped). Verify Approve/confirm disabled until reason entered when mandatory.
- **Partial rejection selection:** cannot proceed with **zero** selected; multi-select works; unselected become approved; Cancel/Back applies no changes.
- **Approve is always full-claim** — no partial approve path.
- **Reject scope depends on entry point** — overview/notification/inbox force full-claim; only detail allows partial. Verify the selection screen is **not** reachable from the overview.
- **Multi-currency claims:** card total must render one or multiple currencies correctly.
- **State transitions:** Pending → Approved (removed from pending); Pending → Rejected/Returned (removed from pending). On any error, claim **stays Pending**.
- **Error/network paths:** backend error keeps claim pending; from detail, a failed action should keep the manager on-screen with a fail toast (per Generic Approvals; confirm for Claims).
- **Empty state** on overview when no pending claims.
- **Idempotency / already-actioned:** behavior if a claim was already approved/rejected elsewhere (e.g. from notification while overview open) is not specified — worth testing.
- **Character limits:** Generic Approvals comment fields cap at **300 chars** with a live counter — confirm whether Claims shares this.

### Generic Approvals patterns (shared UX — may not apply verbatim to Claims)
- Approve from overview uses **checkbox multi-select** → bottom action bar; `approveCommentUse = Mandatory` shows reason modal (max 300 chars, button disabled until entered); `Optional`/`Prohibited` skip it.
- Reject always shows a **rejection reason modal**; reject button disabled only when `rejectionCommentUse = mandatory` and empty.
- Success/fail **toasts** at top of list; from **detail**, a failed action keeps the user on the detail screen (success returns to list).
- Category screen uses `hasPendingApprovals` flag and an "Action required" tag; endpoints `genericapprovals/.../approve` and `.../reject`.

## Open questions / gaps
- **Claim detail field inventory** (expense rows, amounts, **attachments**, **VAT**, dates, net/tax): not enumerated in approval pages — inherited from the employee claim detail screen (not in this scope).
- **Approver comment character limit for Claims:** unspecified; Generic Approvals uses 300.
- **Reject comment necessity — inconsistency:** User Action = comment screen *always* shown, reason *mandatory*; Reject flow / overview UI = shown only "when optional or mandatory." Needs clarification.
- **Requester-side notifications:** content, channel (push/email/inbox), and what the requester can do with a returned/rejected claim (resubmit? edit rejected expenses only?) not described.
- **Partial-rejection resulting claim state:** whether unselected (approved) expenses are finalized immediately while the claim returns to the employee, or the whole claim reverts, is not stated.
- **Claims root page** and a "Rules & Behavior (Approval process)" page returned no content — likely hold canonical state-machine and validation rules.
